-- title:
--   Powers of logarithmic center ideals annihilate strict weighted jets
-- statement:
--   Let $c_j$ be a finite family of complex centers, $v_i\ge0$ the jet weights, $T_i$ logarithm truncation orders, and $e_i$ nonnegative integer powers. Assume $v_{i+1}\le T_i v_0$ and $R\le e_i v_i$ for every coordinate. Put $u_0=X_0-1$ and $u_{i+1}=X_{i+1}-c_{j,i}-(\log(1+u_0))_{<T_i}$ at center $j$, and let $I$ be the product over centers of the ideals generated by $u_i^{e_i}$. Then
--   $$P\in I^n\quad\Longrightarrow\quad [Z^a]\operatorname{formalJet}_{c_j}(P)=0\quad\text{whenever}\quad\sum_i v_i a_i<nR.$$
--   The conclusion is uniform in the polynomial, center, and strict row index. It is the algebraic bridge from congruence modulo the geometric center ideal to equality of logarithmic packets. The real-weight formulation adapts the source's rational-weight vanishing lemma; its weighted filtration argument uses only the displayed inequalities.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/OAI/NumberTheory/PiExponent/Jets/CompactLogJetIdeal.lean, polynomialIdeal and formalJet_packet_zero_of_mem_polynomialIdeal_pow; Jets/CompactJetPolynomial.lean, formalJet_packet_zero_of_mem_pow. Adapted to real weights and individual coefficients.

import Definitions.Def_OAI_PiExponent_LogarithmicCenterIdeals

open Filter Topology
open OAI.PiExponent OAI.PiExponent.DeterminantContradiction

theorem OAI.PiExponent.FormalInterpolation.logarithmic_ideal_power_annihilates_strict_jets
    {m K : ℕ} (c : Fin K → Fin m → ℂ) (T : Fin m → ℕ)
    (e : Fin (m + 1) → ℕ) (v : Fin (m + 1) → ℝ)
    (hv : ∀ i, 0 ≤ v i)
    (hT : ∀ i, v i.succ ≤ (T i : ℝ) * v 0)
    (R : ℝ) (he : ∀ i, R ≤ (e i : ℝ) * v i)
    (n : ℕ) (P : MvPolynomial (Fin (m + 1)) ℂ)
    (hP : P ∈ FormalInterpolation.logarithmicCentersIdeal c T e ^ n)
    (j : Fin K) (a : ↥(strictWeightedSimplex v ((n : ℝ) * R))) :
    MvPowerSeries.coeff (InterpolationMatrix.exponentVector a.val)
      (FormalInterpolation.formalJet (c j) P) = 0 := by sorry
